# valgrind suppressions for tmux (gym/valgrind/vg-tmux).
#
# No library noise needs suppressing: on Ubuntu 24.04 aarch64 (glibc 2.39,
# libevent 2.1.12, ncurses 6.4) the server and clients report no errors from
# those libraries, and only definite and indirect leaks are reported (memory
# still reachable at exit, such as the global options and terminfo, is not).
# Each entry says why what it hides is not a defect.

# A pane's child between fork and exec: environ_push replaces environ (the
# old one is the parent's copy), and if exec fails the child exits at once.
# Nothing is lost in the server, which has its own environ.
{
   pane-child-environ-before-exec
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:calloc
   fun:xcalloc
   fun:environ_push
   fun:spawn_pane
}
